  "findings": [
    "IN_PROGRESS requests within TTL explicitly proceed concurrently; no singleflight or wait-for-result semantics. This is intentional source behavior, not runtime reproduction.",
    "Key includes only configured extracted fields; no mandatory route/method/tenant namespace in guard. Missing selected fields become undefined and disappear during JSON serialization; scope must be explicitly defined.",
    "Storage adapter documentation recommends unique key but handlers append retry and duplicate-attempt records with the same key; concrete constraint design must reconcile both requirements. No adapter runtime evaluated.",
    "Interceptor updates state asynchronously without awaiting persistence; crashes/write failures can leave stale state, and updates use key rather than attempt identity.",
    "TTL retirement does not cancel the original handler; late completion can race subsequent attempt updates. Source-only concern.",
    "Unknown state logs and passes through without stamping a key, so interceptor skips recording.",
    "Canonical JSON has depth limit50 but no width/serialized-size budget; semantics are request fields, not byte-level file equality.",
    "All tracked src files are now fully read; tests/docs/lock review still incomplete.",
    "Public decorator does not invoke exported registration validator. Module validator checks neither inProgressTtl range nor numeric finiteness.",
    "Options interface documents default TTL30000ms, implementation constant10000ms.",
    "keyName is accepted in metadata but unused by reviewed guard/extractor/interceptor; no key namespace contribution.",
    "Mock adapter findByKey returns first COMPLETED-or-IN_PROGRESS match, not strict COMPLETED priority over IN_PROGRESS as abstract contract specifies.",
    "Mock adapter explicitly allows multiple same-key records and has no atomic reservation, so its sequential contract tests cannot prove concurrency safety.",
    "Seven performance callbacks only compare mean helper latency to loose absolute limits; no end-to-end deduplication throughput, tail latency or controlled before/after evidence. No performance test executed.",
    "Runtime helper controls confirm missing different fields collapse, configured header spelling affects key, NaN/null coincide, and different Date timestamps collapse. Last two concern non-JSON typed inputs; plain parsed JSON has no NaN or Date values.",
    "Original hash/extractor/metadata callbacks68/68 pass in isolated adapter; this does not establish atomic reservation, durable state, Nest lifecycle, adapter correctness, or file identity."
  ],
